    "According to you, how can LLMs be used to innovate math learning in schools and universities?": "LLMs can personalize learning by adapting to students’ pace and style. They offer instant explanations, generate practice problems, and clarify misconceptions. In classrooms, they can support teachers with lesson planning and provide students with 24/7 tutoring. With proper guidance, they make math more accessible, especially for those who struggle with traditional methods or feel intimidated."
